$ chap help
exit: 0
--- request
(none)
--- stdout
usage: chap <command> [flags]

commands:
  logo               show the CHAPERONE banner
  mcp                serve the ops as MCP tools over stdio (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor)
  version
  approve list       list your own approval requests (approving is done in the console)
  ci report          post a finished ci run's result to GitHub as a check run (orchestrator only)
  deploy             deploy a commit to the pilot (needs one approval)
  dev-token          mint an interim run token into a file (orchestrator only)
  doctor             check the server's Chaperone install (from a normal, not elevated, terminal)
  drive share        share one Drive file with allowlisted recipients (needs approval)
  git setup          route git's GitHub traffic through chapd's git proxy
  health             read the pilot's readiness status
  intake comment     comment on a labelled operator-board item
  intake list        list the board items labelled for the orchestrator
  intake move        move a labelled operator-board item to a listed state
  intake states      list the board team's states and which a move may use
  issue comment      comment on an issue (GitHub: labelled source:error-watcher; Linear: policy)
  issue get          read one Linear issue of the project's issue team
  issue label        add or remove one label from the policy's list
  issue link         attach a link from a listed host to a Linear issue
  issue list         list Linear issues of the issue team, one page at a time
  issue move         move a Linear issue to a state the policy lists
  issue open         open an issue labelled source:error-watcher
  issue reopen       reopen an issue labelled source:error-watcher
  ledger verify      walk the ledger hash chain, optionally against the signed anchor copies (orchestrator only)
  logs               read recent log lines from a fixed source
  mail send          send one email to allowlisted recipients (needs approval)
  manual             what this caller may ask for, with usage
  op show            show one op, optionally waiting for it to change
  pr checks          read the check runs on a PR's head commit (orchestrator only)
  pr diff            read a PR's unified diff, capped at 256 KiB (orchestrator only)
  pr files           list a PR's changed files, one page at a time (orchestrator only)
  pr merge           merge a PR when verify is green on its exact head
  pr open            open a pull request from the run's branch
  pr update          update a PR's title or body, or its branch
  pr view            read a PR's title, body, state, head, base, mergeability (orchestrator only)
  request net        ask for network access (a the runner surface)
  request op         create the approval card for an op
  request pkg        ask for a package (a the runner surface)
  request scope      ask for a wider task scope (a the runner surface)
  runs revoke        revoke one run, or every active run (orchestrator only)
  vault status       vault state: names and counts, never a value (orchestrator only)

commands that call chapd take --json (the server's JSON, nothing else on stdout).
token: CHAP_RUN_TOKEN, else the orchestrator token file. chapd: CHAP_URL (default http://127.0.0.1:55398).
exit: 0 ok, 2 usage, 3 denied, 4 auth, 5 op not ok, 6 chapd unavailable, 7 pending, 8 not found or conflict, 1 other.
--- stderr
